sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as Client
    participant Token as Token service
    participant Broker as MQTT broker
    Note over Client: Use published host, port, CA and role-specific token origin
    Client->>Token: mTLS POST /request_token (scope, devid)
    alt Identity and entitlement accepted
        Token-->>Client: 200 access_token and mqtt metadata
        Client->>Broker: TLS then MQTT CONNECT (returned credentials)
        Broker-->>Client: CONNACK
        Client->>Broker: SUBSCRIBE $vc/devices/device-1/shadow/name/tutorial/get/accepted and get/rejected
        alt Exact subscriptions authorized
            Broker-->>Client: SUBACK success
            Client->>Broker: PUBLISH $vc/devices/device-1/shadow/name/tutorial/get
            Broker-->>Client: PUBACK (transport only)
            Broker-->>Client: get/accepted or get/rejected from Shadow service
        else Subscription denied
            Broker-->>Client: SUBACK rejection or connection closure per policy
        end
    else Identity or policy rejected
        Token-->>Client: TLS failure or HTTP error
        Note over Client: Resolve identity, activation and capabilities separately
    end
